WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.040
<i>Finally, these scoundrels...</i>

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.780
<i>...have bared their fangs!</i>

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.840
<i>We barely reach the island...</i>

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.870
<i>...and the battle begins!</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.300
<i>There's only eight of us!</i>

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.600
<i>The mutineers led by Silver are twenty in number.</i>

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.640
<i>Once on land, we run for the fort.</i>

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.520
<i>Twenty against eight.</i>

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.230
<i>If we manage to reach the fort,</i>

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.450
<i>we have a chance to take control!</i>

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.930
Treasure
Island

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.730
Takarajima

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.540
saa ikou

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.540
Come, let's go

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.630
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.630
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.470
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.470
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.350
umi hedeyou

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.350
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.270
ikute ni wa

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.270
Many of us

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.270
minna mada shiranai

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.270
Still don't know of

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.020
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.020
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.520
matte iru darou

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.520
That await us there

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:30.030
itsumo shinji you

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:30.030
We must always have trust

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.280
magokoro wo

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.280
And be sincere

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:39.540
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:39.540
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.670
tade hitotsu no

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.670
I only...

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.090
akogare dake wa

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.090
...have one desire

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.380
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.380
And no one...

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:55.090
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:55.090
...will ever take it away

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.640
tade hitotsu no

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.640
I only...

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.940
akogare dake wa

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.940
...have one desire

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.270
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.270
And no one...

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:14.200
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:14.200
...will ever take it away

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:25.210
episode

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:25.210
The Old Man's
\h             Little Bell

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:35.960
Get 'em!

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.090
Watch out!

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.210
Go!

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.030
FIRE!

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.420
Good!

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.350
We're counting on you, Joyce!

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.590
Leave it to me!

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.260
Take careful aim, mates.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.430
If they ever reach the fort,
it'll complicate things.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.310
Fire!

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.530
Darn...
You missed.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.120
Hurry, this way!

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:55.330
Damn it.
You're all a bunch of idiots!

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.800
I'll show you how it's done.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:08.600
<i>Oh no, Father's spyglass!</i>

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.220
Jim, watch out!
Get back here!

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.370
Listen everyone! We're going to return to the ship...

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.540
...and think of a new plan!

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.460
Joyce, hurry yourself to guard duty!

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:36.850
Yes, sir!

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.590
Gray, you too!

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:39.420
Okay.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:43.890
The rest of you, put the supplies in the cabin, then inspect the fort.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:44.840
Aye, sir!

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:44.840
Aye, sir!

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:45.760
Aye-aye!

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:50.370
<i>Upon entering the fort,
the ground rose sharply.</i>

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.640
<i>The cabin is found at the top.</i>

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.600
<i>The cabin was rather big.</i>

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:58.900
<i>In a corner we found a fireplace.</i>

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.810
<i>There's even a well at the back.</i>

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:05.220
<i>Thanks to it, our concerns about drinking water were settled.</i>

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.460
<i>Our little group,
lead by the Captain Smollett,</i>

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.990
<i>was composed of Dr. Livesey and Mr. Trelawney;</i>

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.460
<i>Gray, who's been with us
since we arrived on shore;</i>

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.920
<i>Joyce, who worked for Mr. Trelawney;</i>

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:21.730
<i>Joyce's younger brother, Hunter;</i>

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:24.090
<i>Lastly, good old Redruth...</i>

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.480
<i>...and myself, Jim Hawkins.</i>

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:29.290
<i>If we included Benbow,</i>

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:31.700
<i>we'd be eight men and one animal!</i>

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:36.010
We're going to organize surveillance teams.

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:39.650
We must be on guard at
all times—day and night!

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.970
<i>Without delay, we held a council of war.</i>

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.850
Welcome aboard, leader.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:01.170
Welcome aboard, leader.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:01.170
Welcome aboard, leader.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:04.880
Hey, Hands.
Enough with the "leader" stuff.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.810
It's far too common.

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:09.610
From now on, call me Captain Silver.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.530
Yes, Captain Silver.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.510
Very well, understood.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:18.940
One of you go into my cabin and bring me my captain's uniform.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:19.520
Aye!

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.890
It's a heavy task,

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:24.940
but I must succeed the great Flint.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.780
We're counting on you.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.700
We're counting on you.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:32.660
We're counting on you, Captain!

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:32.660
We're counting on you!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.850
Very good, guys!

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:36.580
Hoist the jolly roger!

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.350
Th-The skull and crossbones!

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:00.310
They've raised the pirate flag
on the Hispaniola!

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:03.390
They did what?!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:17.290
Damn! How dare they do that to our Hispaniola!

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.190
Jim, look at the stern.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.830
There's something even more disgraceful.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:32.510
Silver is taking this seriously.
He's put on the captain's uniform.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:37.140
O Lord! Guide the footsteps of Captain Silver.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.750
To Captain Silver!
Hurray!

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:43.650
To Captain Silver!
Hurray!

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.570
Hurray! Hurray!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:48.370
Who does he think he is?!

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.320
He's just the leader of some pirates!

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.530
Silver you're an idiot!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.800
You're nothing but an idiot!
A big idiot!

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.420
Captain Smollett!

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.420
Captain Smollett!

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:11.210
It's not that I want to respond to their jolly roger,

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:14.730
but we're staking our lives on this fort.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:17.970
I swear on the Union Jack to fight with honour!

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:35.010
Captain Silver, it's the Union Jack!

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:38.970
I can see that. They seem as determined as we are.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:42.290
At least that gives us an attractive target.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:46.130
Hey, let's send our regards.
Give that Union Jack a proper salute.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:05.100
Fire! Fire! Fire! Fire!

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:13.450
Captain Smollett, they must be targetting our flag!

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.530
It has to be taken down!
At once!

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:19.950
No! That's out of the question! The Union Jack is our pride!

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:23.590
Taking it down again signals our defeat.

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:26.920
You're right.
I'm sorry I panicked.

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:34.140
<i>Yes, I too, refuse to lower the flag!</i>

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:37.850
<i>It would be humiliating to surrender to the pirates...</i>

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:39.850
<i>...and admit defeat to Silver!</i>

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.780
Take cover!
T-Take cover!

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:57.860
Cease fire!

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:04.000
I think that'll do for greetings.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.940
This is where the real battle
is about to begin.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:22.760
<i>We spent the first night
in the shelter of the fort.</i>

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:27.130
<i>Benbow and I were on guard duty.</i>

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:29.350
<i>Together with old Redruth.</i>

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.610
What a sweet sound.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:38.400
Much better than cannons and guns.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:42.010
Even though the enemy could attack us at any moment...

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:43.730
You're taking it easy?

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:45.040
Don't say that, Jim.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:48.490
The men who listen to
the chiming of this bell...

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:51.690
...are the same ones who fight,
kill each other...

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:56.300
...or betray their friends.
Yes, we're the same.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.880
Men are very strange beings.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:30.710
Silver and I were never friends!

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:56.610
Our initial plan was to wait until they uncovered the treasure.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:12:00.110
Then, we would have attacked them and split the treasure.

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:03.150
However, now that our identities have been uncovered,

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:05.570
we're going to change the plan.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:12.610
Basically, while we're watching,
they won't try to find the treasure.

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:15.380
The most important thing is to get that map.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:18.510
Once we have the map we can search for the treasure.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:22.170
Captain, that whale Trelawney has it!

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.970
No, it must be Livesey!

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:27.970
Could it be Smollett?
He's their leader, right?

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:31.450
And what about that little brat, Jim?

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:34.450
Now, now.
Those are just guesses.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:37.530
Anyway, we're going to the island tonight.

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:41.400
It'll take time to overcome this fort.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:44.710
Those I call will stay and guard the ship.

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:48.530
Quarter Master Hands, you'll be in charge of this group.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:50.290
Yes, sir, leave it to me.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.770
Red Cap, you stay on board.

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:53.640
Aye.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.720
You too, Gaunt Dog.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:57.260
Aye-aye, sir.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:01.250
And you, Sam Ironarms,
will be first mate to Hands.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.690
Understood.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:05.730
Very good.
The rest of you come with me.

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:07.810
Yes, Captain Silver!

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.450
Hey, Jim!

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.030
Wake up!
I've brought you some hot soup.

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:30.350
It's good.

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:35.060
Tell me, Jim. Do you think that
they're going to attack tonight?

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:40.230
Don't think so.
It's been a rough day.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:42.960
Surely they're exhausted.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:46.950
I agree with you, but that Silver...

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:50.890
No one can predict what he'll do.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.270
That Ben Gunn you met...

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:56.420
...seemed to fear the wrath of Silver, too.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:07.310
Don't fall asleep, Jim.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:10.490
Our comrades trust us with their lives.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:22.630
In this world there are
different kinds of treasures.

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:25.800
For example, the treasure
that's hidden on this island,

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.720
belongs to Flint.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:31.240
And your mother,
that you left at Black Hill,

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.520
has a treasure of her own.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:35.490
Really? I didn't know.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:39.020
It's you, of course!
You are your mother's treasure!

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.900
I see, that's what you meant.

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:45.280
Mine is this bell.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.800
When Mr. Trelawney was just a baby,

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:54.080
I used this bell to soothe him.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:58.210
The admirable man we know today was such a cry-baby.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.760
But when I rang this bell,

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:03.170
he'd stop crying and smile at me.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:07.600
I never get tired of his wonderful smile.

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:10.130
Since then, this bell has been my treasure.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:14.100
So it's also a treasure for Mr. Trelawney.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:18.640
No, no. I highly doubt
he remembers my bell.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.010
After all, he was a baby at the time.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:30.070
It's freezing cold...

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:31.910
What's the matter, Gray?
Can't sleep?

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:35.040
I forgot to clean my knives.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:38.950
I see... It's normal to be a little out of it on a night like this.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:50.550
Jim.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:51.260
What is it?

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.800
What is your treasure?

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.840
What, my treasure?

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:59.960
Let's see...
I'd say...

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.140
My father's spyglass.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:06.570
And the Admiral Benbow Inn that's kept by my mother.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.530
But my most precious treasure is my mother, of course.

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:12.670
What else is there?
Let me think...

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:14.990
Of course, I forgot!

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:18.450
Lily is also one of my treasures.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:27.620
That's great, Jim.
You have a lot of treasures.

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.480
No, not really.

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:34.140
Since you have so many, why do you want Flint's?

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:39.840
That's obvious. The more you have the better!

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:42.940
I see.
Well, I suppose you're right.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:55.280
I would've liked to keep as many treasures as you do in old age.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:00.160
But alas, when we become adults,

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:05.790
we lose our treasures one after
the other and don't even realize it.

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:27.600
What was that?

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:28.020
They're here!

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.980
Forward, men!

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:45.910
Bastards!

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:52.270
Jim, get down!
Return to the cabin!

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.270
Come on Jim, hurry!

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.370
Break down the door!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:24.830
Yeah!

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:30.830
Jim, hurry!

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:31.920
Yes, yes, yes!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:32.880
Here, done!

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:38.090
Go on, do it!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.240
With pleasure.

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:45.100
Roast them like pigs!

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:56.800
I see no flames, so I'd say they've failed.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:59.780
Very well, we're leaving. Puppy, give the signal.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:01.110
Right.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:38.990
Redruth, forgive me.

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:42.950
I should never have taken you to such a place.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:49.880
Somehow, this ringing sounds familiar to me.

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:53.080
He treasured it for a very long time.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:57.100
Really? That old kook.

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:59.090
Redruth...

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:09.600
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:14.560
Jim, what's going on?
Where are you going?

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:16.430
Don't worry, I'll follow him.

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:32.280
Captain Silver, we have two wounded.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:33.680
The others are fine.

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:35.510
I see, that's good to hear.

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:38.440
By the way, Captain,
something's bothering me.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:40.840
What?
Something bothering you?

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:44.810
Yes, three of our men are suffering from a very strange fever.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:46.260
A fever?

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:51.640
What happened to them?

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:54.200
Aye, sir.
According to them,

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:56.310
they were bitten by mosquitoes.

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:57.900
What, mosquitoes?

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:58.570
Aye.

00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:02.810
This is bad...
They must've caught malaria.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:06.360
Captain, where are you going?

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.320
On a walk.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:09.550
I have to think of a plan.

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:19.170
I've found you!

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:28.550
Jim, it's been a long time.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:37.060
That has a nice ring.

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:45.110
One of your men shot
and killed old Redruth!

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:48.710
I see.
And thus, you're going to shoot me?

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:49.990
That's right!

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:52.950
Go ahead.
Shoot if you want to.

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:01.340
That's really a beautiful ring.

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:18.190
Damn it! Damn it!
Damn it all!

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:31.830
To      be        continued

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:37.950
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:37.950
Hey sea breeze

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:43.760
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:43.760
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:49.970
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:49.970
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:49.970 --> 00:22:55.410
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:49.970 --> 00:22:55.410
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.410 --> 00:23:00.820
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.410 --> 00:23:00.820
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:06.280
kaban ippai no

00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:06.280
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:11.910
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:11.910
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:17.770
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:17.770
Will be brought back

00:23:18.860 --> 00:23:24.360
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:18.860 --> 00:23:24.360
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:30.250
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:30.250
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:39.970
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:39.970
I blow out a whistle

00:23:44.680 --> 00:23:46.020
Silver's here!

00:23:46.360 --> 00:23:48.280
He takes the treasure map.

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:50.240
His threatening manner scares me.

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:53.680
We were so close, how sad!

00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:55.960
But I'm going to fight against him!

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:58.440
With the help of Ben Gunn,

00:23:58.440 --> 00:24:01.540
I find myself behind the cannon that threatens us.

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:04.150
But in reality, this is no ordinary cannon.

